contentText:
It&#8217;s been more than two months since Taylor Swift and Travis Kelce crashed all your social feeds with their reportedly lavish, but extremely locked-down wedding at New York&#8217;s Madison Square Garden. Not a single photo of the dress, the ceremony, the afterparty or really any other salient details have leaked from either Swift or Kelce&#8217;s camp in one of the most impressive displays of message discipline in recent pop history.

But on Wednesday (Sept. 2) Travis, 36, is gearing up to spill some tea about the event in the season 5 debut of his New Heights podcast with brother Jason Kelce. In a minute-long preview clip that went up early Wednesday, Jason opens the show by low-keying the event heard &#8217;round the world, saying, &#8220;Interesting bit of the offseason &#8230; you&#8217;re finally married!&#8221;

Travis then proudly holds up his golden wedding band and confirms, &#8220;I am a married man, yep.&#8221; The preview then quickly moves on to shots of the guys laughing uproariously at an unheard joke, Travis shouting &#8220;welcome back!&#8221; to their loyal viewers and Jason amping up the energy even more by screeching, &#8220;HE&#8217;S BACK! S&#8211;T!&#8221;

According to People , during the episode, Travis calls the wedding a &#8220;night out we&#8217;ll never forget,&#8221; adding, &#8220;Me and Taylor are so thankful for everybody that showed up, from the vows to just seeing everyone, to how much fun we had, throughout the entire evening and hearing that, kind of be relayed through everybody’s stories of the night. And it was just so magical, man.”

If he had any regrets, he said, it&#8217;s wishing that the night could have lasted even longer than it did. &#8220;It felt like it just happened in the blink of an eye.&#8221; Kelce and Swift married at MSG on July 3 in a ceremony conducted by comedian and friend Adam Sandler, with Kelce saying they chose the unusual venue because the couple wanted to get married &#8220;somewhere where we could have a very intimate and genuine setting without a lot of distractions. And we needed it to be a private feel.&#8221;

After some light manscaping talk in the preview clip, the brothers also get to another really important topic: the debut of Travis and Taylor&#8217;s adorable Samoyed Wendy in the NFL star&#8217;s new Tommy Hilfiger campaign, which dropped on Tuesday (Sept. 1). In the ad, Kelce is seen dapping up some famous sports stars and musicians as he strides through New York&#8217;s Plaza Hotel on his way to chill in a suite with the white-haired puppy.

&#8220;We were gonna use a dog and am I OK with dogs,&#8221; Travis says in the preview. &#8220;I&#8217;m like, &#8216;I have a dog.&#8217; And like, &#8216;Oh, you wanna bring your dog in?'&#8221; he said the shoot&#8217;s producers asked him. The full episode of New Heights drops at 9:30 a.m. ET on Wednesday.
